--- leap years
1900: FALSE   2000: TRUE
2023: FALSE   2024: TRUE
1: FALSE   4: TRUE
--- days in a month
February 2024: 29  February 1900: 28  February 2000: 29
April: 30  December: 31  January: 31
month 0: 0  month 13: 0
--- what is a date, and what is a time
2024-02-29: TRUE   2023-02-29: FALSE
0000-01-01: FALSE   10000-01-01: FALSE
2024-13-01: FALSE   2024-04-31: FALSE
23:59:59: TRUE   24:00:00: FALSE   00:00:60: FALSE
--- a stamp from six numbers
2024-02-29 13:05:09: 2024-02-29 13:05:09  DateValid TRUE TimeValid TRUE
2023-02-29 00:00:00: failed, outside the representable range
2024-01-01 24:00:00: failed, outside the representable range
--- the day count, and its two ends
0001-01-01: 1
1970-01-01: 719163
2000-01-01: 730120
2000-03-01: 730180
9999-12-31: 3652059
MinDayNumber is 0001-01-01: TRUE
MaxDayNumber is 9999-12-31: TRUE
--- and back again
day 1: 0001-01-01 00:00:00  DateValid TRUE TimeValid FALSE
day 719163: 1970-01-01 00:00:00  DateValid TRUE TimeValid FALSE
day 730180: 2000-03-01 00:00:00  DateValid TRUE TimeValid FALSE
day 3652059: 9999-12-31 00:00:00  DateValid TRUE TimeValid FALSE
day 0: failed, outside the representable range
day 3652060: failed, outside the representable range
--- every day of a leap February round-trips
1 February plus 28: 2024-02-29 00:00:00  DateValid TRUE TimeValid FALSE
--- adding and subtracting days
2024-02-28 + 1: 2024-02-29 12:00:00  DateValid TRUE TimeValid TRUE
2023-02-28 + 1: 2023-03-01 12:00:00  DateValid TRUE TimeValid TRUE
1900-02-28 + 1: 1900-03-01 12:00:00  DateValid TRUE TimeValid TRUE
2000-02-28 + 1: 2000-02-29 12:00:00  DateValid TRUE TimeValid TRUE
2024-12-31 + 1: 2025-01-01 23:59:59  DateValid TRUE TimeValid TRUE
2000-03-01 - 1: 2000-02-29 00:00:00  DateValid TRUE TimeValid TRUE
2024-01-01 + 366: 2025-01-01 00:00:00  DateValid TRUE TimeValid TRUE
9999-12-31 + 1: failed, outside the representable range
0001-01-01 - 1: failed, outside the representable range
0001-01-01 - maxint: failed, outside the representable range
--- the difference between two dates
1970-01-01 to 2000-01-01: 10957
2000-01-01 to 1970-01-01: -10957
2024-01-01 to 2025-01-01: 366
2023-01-01 to 2024-01-01: 365
a day is a day whatever the hour: 1
--- which day of the week
day 1 (0001-01-01): Monday
day 719163 (1970-01-01): Thursday
day 730120 (2000-01-01): Saturday
day 730180 (2000-03-01): Wednesday
day 3652059 (9999-12-31): Friday
a week from day 1: Monday Tuesday Wednesday Thursday Friday Saturday Sunday
day 0: Sunday   day -6: Monday
--- which day of the year
2024-03-01: 61
2023-03-01: 60
2024-01-01: 1
2024-12-31: 366
2023-12-31: 365
--- writing one, and reading it back
2024-02-29 13:05:09: [2024-02-29T13:05:09]
0001-01-01 00:00:00: [0001-01-01T00:00:00]
parse 2024-02-29T13:05:09: 2024-02-29 13:05:09  DateValid TRUE TimeValid TRUE
parse with a space: 2024-02-29 13:05:09  DateValid TRUE TimeValid TRUE
parse a date alone: 2024-02-29 00:00:00  DateValid TRUE TimeValid FALSE
parse a time alone: 0001-01-01 13:05:09  DateValid FALSE TimeValid TRUE
round trip: [2024-02-29T13:05:09]
the round trip is exact: TRUE
--- what a parse refuses, and with which code
2023-02-29: failed, outside the representable range
2024-13-01: failed, outside the representable range
2024-02-29T25:00:00: failed, outside the representable range
13:05:60: failed, outside the representable range
2024/02/29: failed, not of the expected form
20xx-02-29: failed, not of the expected form
2024-02-29X13:05:09: failed, not of the expected form
a leading space: failed, not of the expected form
the empty string: failed, not of the expected form
a zone designator: failed, not of the expected form
--- an offset, which is all a zone is here
13:05 at -60: 2024-02-29 12:05:09  DateValid TRUE TimeValid TRUE
00:30 at -60: 2024-02-28 23:30:00  DateValid TRUE TimeValid TRUE
23:30 at +60: 2024-03-01 00:30:00  DateValid TRUE TimeValid TRUE
00:00 at +330: 2024-03-01 05:30:00  DateValid TRUE TimeValid TRUE
back again: 2024-02-29 00:00:00  DateValid TRUE TimeValid TRUE
at +0: 2024-02-29 13:05:09  DateValid TRUE TimeValid TRUE
at +1440: failed, outside the representable range
at -1440: failed, outside the representable range
past the last day: failed, outside the representable range
--- a stamp that says its date means nothing
day number of a time: failed, not present
a day added to a time: failed, not present
a time formatted whole: failed, not present
a time shifted: failed, not present
a date formatted whole: failed, not present
a date shifted: failed, not present
a time to a date: failed, not present
a date to a time: failed, not present
--- fields that are in their subranges and are still not a date
day number: failed, outside the representable range
formatted: failed, outside the representable range
a day added: failed, outside the representable range
day of the year: failed, outside the representable range
shifted: failed, outside the representable range
a year with no representation: failed, outside the representable range
--- the clock, which is the one thing that cannot be printed
the clock is a day this module can count: TRUE
